{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdho6BVa8pUjZyQmYAmN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with the verdict **upheld**: I found no way to break any of the four B07 checks. I only read files and did not run any code, so this comes from reading the source, not from running the tests.\n\n- **B07.1 holds.** `config/policy.yaml:40-45` gives finite values for all six per-run limits (steps, wall seconds, tokens, cost, tool calls per minute, sub-agents). The `while True` loop in `app/loop.py` is capped by `budget.check_step()`.\n- **B07.2 holds.** The limits are enforced in harness code, and the model has no tool that can change them. `execute_tool` re-raises `BudgetExceeded` instead of swallowing it. The handler at `app/loop.py:175` records it, posts to the ops channel and returns `None`.\n- **B07.3 holds.** The extractor sub-agent charges the parent's `Budget` object, and `budget.check_subagent()` caps how many can start. Its role has no `extract_line_items` tool, so it can't start another sub-agent, and its own loop is limited to 4 turns.\n- **B07.4 holds.** Daily spend quotas and per-minute run-start limits are kept per user, tenant and fleet in Postgres (`spend_quota` and `run_start_window`). They persist across runs, and going over a limit raises `BudgetExceeded`.\n\nOne minor weakness, which I didn't treat as a failure: the wall-clock limit is only checked at the start of each step. A single slow step can run past 300 seconds, but the run still stops at the next check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":997,"cache_read_input_tokens":26247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":997},"output_tokens":518,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pare